                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237389518",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198388606792",
                            "num_reviews": 1286,
                            "playtime_forever": 383,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 383,
                            "last_played": 1791649618
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You get what you pay for. I didn't expect much from this game, yet I was left disappointed. I'm not going to cry over 2 bucks, those mixed reviews are totally justifed tho.\n\nFirst of all, it requires a bit of legwork to get the game running on a modern system, you need to disable steam cloud or else the game doesn't save, then you need to go to the control panel to change a few settings and cap it at 60fps, and lastly turn off vsync - not a big deal. \n\nHowever, the game itself is so repetitive. It's nice there are a ton of cars, different gamemodes and seemingly endless content but then you realize you're driving across the same sterile maps over and over again. The physics are odd and so is the handling, it's like you're on ice, the vehicles are prone to spinning out as well. No matter what terrain you race on, it doesn't make a huge difference. everything felt like gravel to me. At least the graphics aged well for a decade old game.",
